Resumania is a resume-building library. It is not necessarily meant to be
extremely customizable, but rather a tool to create more procedural resumes, and
rigid enough that you can make multiple variant resumes from mostly the same set
of information, just swapping out parts as needed.

The motivation behind this is mostly to be able to capture *all* the information
that a person wants in any number of resumes in a common manner and then be able
to easily create multiple tailored resumes without having to re-write a lot of
the same information or boilerplate.

Navigating this project:

- The main source for the library is in 'src/', with the primary elements of the
  resume each having their own file within 'src/'.
- 'version' simply contains the text of the current version number of the
  package. This is mainly for scripting purposes (e.g. when creating the built
  package).
- Tests are located in 'test/', with each file acting as a standalone document
  to assist with visually debugging/testing changes to the package. They serve
  more as examples and manual/visual checks than actual pass/fail kind of test
  for now.
- The 'template/' directory contains a template that Typst can use to generate a
  new project from.
- The 'assets/' directory contains extra files that will be included in the
  built package, such as a 'README.md'.

Related/similar projects:
    - basic-resume: https://github.com/stuxf/basic-typst-resume-template
    - min-resume: https://github.com/mayconfmelo/min-resume

